Nora introduces herself
=======================

With no conversation history there is nothing on screen but a heading and some suggestion cards, so
the first thing a new person meets is a menu rather than a person. This adds — it replaces nothing —
an introduction card under the heading, shown only when there are no conversations yet:

> **Hi — I'm Nora.**
> You're new here, so: what do I call you?
> I'm an aide that runs on this machine — your machine — for you, one user. I keep a memory folder
> you own, so the next session does not start from nothing. Nothing here is locked to an account, and
> every part of it can be changed or deleted later.

The persona says the same thing in its own words, in the register that matches the theme: *"Hi — I'm
Nora. You're new here, so: what do I call you?"* by default, *"Sup, bitches — I'm Nora…"* in his own.
Two sentences about what she is, then the question. The card disappears the moment there is a
conversation to show instead.

